# Enterprise Edit Mode v2

Canonical references:

- `docs/06-guidelines/NEXORA_PLATFORM_UX_CONSTITUTION.md` (sections 7–8)
- `docs/06-guidelines/EDIT_MODE_V2_STANDARD.md`
- `docs/06-guidelines/INLINE_EDITING_STANDARD.md`

## Core Principle

Profile and detail pages have two modes only: **View** and **Edit**.

- View Mode: one **Edit** action.
- Edit Mode: inline editors + **Cancel** / **Save Changes** with **Unsaved changes** indicator.

List pages keep the modal pattern (`RecordFormDialog`).

## Required Platform Components

Use shared components from `@/shared/ui`:

- `EditablePage` — page-level View/Edit bar, batch save, workflow dialog
- `EditableProfileWorkspace` — profile sections on top of `EditablePage`
- `EditableSectionCard`, `EditableFieldGrid`, `EditableField`
- `useEditablePage` — draft state, changed fields, keyboard shortcuts
- `CrossEngineLookupWorkflow` — generic lookup workflow dialog
- `EntityLookup`, `DatePicker` / `DatePickerField`
- `platform.feedback` — success/error toasts

## Field Ownership

| Ownership | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| `entity` | Direct inline edit, batch save |
| `versioned` | Inline edit, versioned save semantics |
| `cross-engine` | **Change** opens in-page workflow modal via `renderWorkflow` |
| `readonly` | Visible, muted, lock when denied |

Never use `workflowHref` or `router.push` for cross-engine edits.

## Save Rules

- One **Save Changes** saves all changed entity/versioned fields together.
- Use `saveStrategy="changed-only"` only for patch endpoints.
- **Cancel** restores original values.
- Unsaved navigation shows **Save Changes**, **Discard**, **Continue Editing**.

## Prohibited

- Full-page edit navigation for profile/detail fields
- Module-local edit mode implementations
- Native date inputs
- Cross-engine field mutation without workflow dialog
- Hiding data when permission is denied

## New Screens

Every new profile/detail workspace across all business apps must use Edit Mode v2.
